From 910ffbe862893010f9fc22387c5f2423f2b0448a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 09:11:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] logging: add runtime metadata provider support

Introduce a runtime metadata provider framework that allows
extensions to contribute metadata during log creation.

Unlike plugin extension hooks, which operate on plugin
requests, runtime metadata providers operate on the log
creation path and enable metadata enrichment without
requiring changes to event producers.

Registered providers receive log creation context and
may append runtime-derived metadata to a shared JSON
object. The aggregated metadata is stored in log
additional data for subsequent consumption by plugin
extensions or other framework components.

This establishes a generic runtime enrichment mechanism
while preserving existing plugin processing, descriptor
generation, and lifecycle management flows.

Change-Id: I069bb5d230ae965fe1d9cd4c1bba1b69c7f76e03
Signed-off-by: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
---
